B.4
Conditional moments
The related concept of conditional probability dates back from Laplace who calculated conditional distributions. Kolmogorov [1933] formalised it by using the Radon-Nikodym theorem. Halmos and Doob [1953] generalised the
conditional expectation by using sub-sigma-algebras.
