B.10
Some random sampling
For details see text book by Rice [1995]. We assume that the population is of size N and that associated with
each member of the population is a numerical value of interest denoted by x1, x2, .., xN. The variable xi may be a
numerical variable such as age or weight, or it may take on the value 1 or 0 to denote the presence or absence of some
characteristic. The latter is called the dichotomous case.
