C.2.4
Combining linear generators
Combining parallel multiple recursive sequences provides an efﬁcient way of implementing random number generators
with long periods and good structural properties. However, combining elements with distinct prime moduli leads to
another MRG with non-prime modulus m equal to the product of the moduli of the components, and the period can
be up to half the product of the component’s periods. One approach combines J copies of Equation (C.2.2)
