The statistic ˆφk,k is called the kth sample partial autocorrelation coefﬁcient (PACF). If the process Xt is genuinely
ARppq then the population PACF ˆφk,k is exactly zero for all k ¡ p. Thus a diagnostic for ARppq is that the sample
PACFs are close to zero for k ¡ p.
