where tWtu is white noise. The modiﬁed model for tXtu is thus an ARMA process with autoregressive and moving
operators φZpBqφpBq and θZpBqθpBq respectively.
The Akaike Information Criterion, AIC (Akaike [1973]), and a bias-corrected version, AICC (Sugiura, 1978;
Hurvich and Tsai [1989]) are two methods for selection of regression and autoregressive models. Both criteria may
be viewed as estimators of the expected Kullback-Leibler information. The main idea is that we want to ﬁt a model
