D.5
ARCH and GARCH models
D.5.1
The ARCH process
Volatility clustering has long been a salient feature of series generated from ﬁnancial data. However, only recently
did researchers in ﬁnance recognise the importance of explicitly modelling time varying second-order moments. One
of the most important and widely used approach is that of the Autoregressive Conditional Heteroskedastic (ARCH)
model introduced by Engle [1982]. Following his seminal paper we deﬁne a zero mean ARCHppq process tXtu by
