D.5.2
The GARCH process
In empirical applications of the ARCH model, a relatively long lag in the conditional variance equation is often called
for. In light of this, Bollerslev extended the ARCH class of models to allow for a longer memory and ﬂexible lag
structure. The Generalised Autoregressive Conditional Heteroskedastic (GARCH) model is deﬁned as
