E.6
Valuation in ﬁnancial markets
First we assume a complete market with a continuum of option prices in the state space. Second, we assume the
existence of a risk-neutral measure under which the expected return on any asset is the risk-free rate, and the existence
of a strictly positive pricing kernel. Then, we assume that the underlying process is Markov in the state variables, and
that we can discretise the state space.
E.6.1
Pricing securities
