A self-ﬁnancing portfolio is a strategy to buy or sell assets whose value is not modiﬁed by adding or removing
cash. Further, the self-ﬁnancing condition implies that the value of the portfolio does not jump at trading dates. The
self-ﬁnancing condition is a necessary and sufﬁcient condition for the continuity process of the value of the portfolio.
