Assumption F.1.2 We assume that there is no arbitrage opportunity between admissible portfolio strategies, in which
case the market is viable.
As a result of the absence of arbitrage opportunity, there is a constraint on the rate of return of ﬁnancial assets. The
riskier the asset, the higher the return, to justify its presence in the portfolio.
