In the M-market the prices of contingent claims are the expected value of their terminal ﬂux. One is then left to
compute the weights of the hedging portfolio when the terminal ﬂux is unknown. In the simple Markowian case of
the Black-Scholes formula the weights are expressed in terms of the gradients of the price which is the expectation
of the derivative of the random variable ΦM with respect to the Markowian variables. In the general case, we need
to compute the weights representing the random variable XT as a stochastic integral with respect to the Brownian
